 act as surfactant, there should be both polar and non-polar ends in the molecules.","difficulty":"Medium","source":"AIIMS 2003","_marksId":"66bb647108a93761696e2c71","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":547,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemistry in Everyday Life","exam":"Medical","examName":"AIIMS","q":"Methyl orange is the example of which type of dye?","options":["Acid dye","Mordant dye","Azo dye","Both (1) and (3)."],"answer":3,"solution":"Methyl orange belongs to the group of azo dyes. It is also acidic in nature due to presence of sulphonic group.\n<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Faiims%252FG5zNZTLyyUVQ34VvC1eue2tpaGndYPmNaFWYMJDvjk4.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Faiims%2FG5zNZTLyyUVQ34VvC1eue2tpaGndYPmNaFWYMJDvjk4.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Faiims%2FG5zNZTLyyUVQ34VvC1eue2tpaGndYPmNaFWYMJDvjk4.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>","difficulty":"Easy","source":"AIIMS 2002","_marksId":"66bb645808a93761696e2bba","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":548,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemistry in Everyday Life","exam":"Medical","examName":"AIIMS","q":"Arsenic drugs are mainly used in the treatment of","options":["Jaundice","Typhoid","Syphilis","Cholera."],"answer":2,"solution":"Arsenic drugs such as salvarsan is used for treatment of syphilis.","difficulty":"Easy","source":"AIIMS 2016","_marksId":"66bb65b308a93761696e3592","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":549,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemistry in Everyday Life","exam":"Medical","examName":"AIIMS","q":"Assertion : Non competitive drugs alter the shape of active site of the enzyme.\nReason : They attack on the active site of enzyme.","options":["If both assertion and reason are true and reason is the correct explanation of assertion.","If both assertion and reason are true but reason is not the correct explanation of assertion.","If assertion is true but reason is false.","If both assertion and reason are false."],"answer":2,"solution":"Non competitive drugs do not bind to the active site but bind to a allosteric site of the enzyme.","difficulty":"Easy","source":"AIIMS 2018 (26 May)","_marksId":"66bb65e508a93761696e36fc","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":550,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemistry in Everyday Life","exam":"Medical","examName":"AIIMS","q":"Which of the following is a narrow spectrum antibiotics?","options":["Tetracycline","Penicillin","Streptomycin","Chloramphenicol"],"answer":1,"solution":"Penicillin has narrow spectrum.","difficulty":"Easy","source":"AIIMS 2019 (25 May)","_marksId":"66bb661708a93761696e3862","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":551,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemistry in Everyday Life","exam":"Medical","examName":"AIIMS","q":"Which is a bactericidal antibiotic?","options":["Penicillin","Erythromycin","Tetracycline","Chloramphenicol"],"answer":0,"solution":"Penicillin is a bactericidal whereas erythromycin, tetracycline and chloramphenicol are bacteriostatic antibiotics.","difficulty":"Easy","source":"AIIMS 2014","_marksId":"66bb658208a93761696e342e","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":552,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemistry in Everyday Life","exam":"Medical","examName":"AIIMS","q":"The pair whose both species are used in antiacid medicinal preparation is","options":["$\\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$ and $\\mathrm{Mg}(\\mathrm{OH})_2$","$\\mathrm{Na}_2 \\mathrm{CO}_3$ and $\\mathrm{Ca}\\left(\\mathrm{HCO}_3\\right)_2$","$\\mathrm{Ca}\\left(\\mathrm{HCO}_3\\right)_2$ and $\\mathrm{Mg}(\\mathrm{OH})_2$","$\\mathrm{Ca}(\\mathrm{OH})_2$ and $\\mathrm{NaHCO}_3$."],"answer":0,"solution":"Intestine is acidic due to formation of $\\mathrm{HCl}$ during digestion. Excessive acidity in the intestine creates problem of intestinal ulcer, gastric reflux and oesophagitis. The compound which reduced or neutralise acidity are called antacids.\n\n\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{NaHCO}_3+\\mathrm{HCl} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{NaCl}+\\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}+\\mathrm{CO}_2 \\\\\n& \\mathrm{Mg}(\\mathrm{OH})_2+2 \\mathrm{HCl} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{MgCl}_2+2 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}\n\\end{aligned}\n","difficulty":"Easy","source":"AIIMS 2006","_marksId":"66bb64ba08a93761696e2e87","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]},{"id":553,"subject":"Chemistry","chapter":"Chemistry in Everyday Life","exam":"Medical","examName":"AIIMS","q":"Which one of the following is not a surfactant?","options":["<img src=\"/api/proxy-image?url=https%3A%2F%2Ffirebasestorage.googleapis.com%2Fv0%2Fb%2Fquantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app%2Fo%2Fquestions%252Ffigs%252Fpyq%252Faiims%252FvgVH6cT9kovLZVdjYTLLsJZk0x4qLLXmVB9AVGCh1GU.original.fullsize.png%3Falt%3Dmedia&clean=1&v=wm2\" data-qx-orig-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Faiims%2FvgVH6cT9kovLZVdjYTLLsJZk0x4qLLXmVB9AVGCh1GU.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\" data-qx-storage-src=\"https://firebasestorage.googleapis.com/v0/b/quantrexacademy-app.firebasestorage.app/o/questions%2Ffigs%2Fpyq%2Faiims%2FvgVH6cT9kovLZVdjYTLLsJZk0x4qLLXmVB9AVGCh1GU.original.fullsize.png?alt=media\"><br>","\\(\\mathrm{CH}_3-\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_2\\right)_{14}-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{NH}_2\\)","\\(\\mathrm{CH}_3-\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_2\\right)_{16}-\\mathrm{CH}_2 \\mathrm{OSO}_2^{-} \\mathrm{Na}^{+}\\)","\\(\\mathrm{OHC}-\\left(\\mathrm{CH}_2\\right)_{14}-\\mathrm{CH}_2-\\mathrm{COO}^{-} \\mathrm{Na}^{+}\\)."],"answer":1,"solution":"Molecule is simply amine in nature.","difficulty":"Easy","source":"AIIMS 2008","_marksId":"66bb64ed08a93761696e2ff4","questionType":"singleCorrect","type":"singleCorrect","_repairLog":["medical_cache_enrich"]}]}